      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "THE PATIENT",
          "content": "We present the very rare case of a pineoblastoma with large central cyst in a 7-year-old boy who presented with a short history of gradually worsening headache and upward gaze palsy."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "UNASSIGNED",
          "Label": "IMAGING INVESTIGATIONS",
          "content": "On CT and MRI studies, it was seen as a peripherally calcified, irregularly shaped mass with heterogeneous low signal intensity on T1-weighted images and ringed enhancement after gadolinium administration; there was homogeneous high signal intensity on T1-weighted images."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "DISCUSSION",
          "content": "We discuss differential diagnosis for several types of cystic tumors in the pineal region, including pineoblastomas."
        }
      ]},
